Do humans understand the world or do they just appear to understand the world? From where I sit I am inclined to say that the extent to which any given human understands the world is rather limited, some a lot more so than others. Do I understand the technology I've spent since 1959 learning and exploiting or an I simply an organic ChatGPT that can focus on the technology it has learned and manipulate it into components for GPS satellites, for one example? I can't say. I can say I do not understand humans in general enough to feel comfortable with all but one specific human being  in my presence. (Autism does that to a person to varying degrees.)

Sometimes turning the question around like that can help you answer the question. Whether ChatGPT really "understands the world", whatever that means, if it can examine what it knows and provide correct answers within that context often enough, it may not matter. Humans might fail the test with (insert your adjective here) regularity, too.

